{"id": "EUVD-2026-99257", "enisaUuid": "3cdedbab-5602-328b-a220-b008e45e9630", "description": "youlai-boot through 2.21.1 contains a missing authorization vulnerability that allows any authenticated user to enable or disable accounts because the updateUserStatus handler lacks a @PreAuthorize check. Attackers can send PATCH requests to /api/v1/users/{userId}/status to disable root or admin accounts, locking administrators out, or re-enable accounts an administrator has disabled.", "datePublished": "2026-10-13T18:50:04", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T22:29:44", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:N/VI:L/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@1ExmmukzRMWN7B4gQ4W-4Q/youlai-boot-role-menu-assignment-and-user-status-missing-authorization", "https://github.com/youlaitech/youlai-boot/blob/v2.21.1/src/main/java/com/youlai/boot/system/controller/UserController.java#L114-L126", "https://github.com/youlaitech/youlai-boot/commit/86a9b3e212ff5a5537b0c7050c7802aea7fe486f", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/youlai-boot-through-2.21.1-missing-authorization-in-user-status-update-endpoint"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-110216", "GHSA-6cm8-g463-wr86"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.44, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "95be66ac-b0ef-31c8-8ca8-444a2f65d37c", "product": {"name": "youlai-boot", "vendor": {"name": "youlaitech"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22642.21.1"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "2b1eeea2-84f1-3fab-958f-8f300c5c9e6a", "vendor": {"name": "youlaitech"}}], "isExploited": false}